  "result": "I found and fixed the bug: `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:34` compared the argument to each item's **name** instead of its **SKU**:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.name != sku]   # before\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]    # after\n```\n\n`'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so the line always stayed in the cart. `Cart.add` already looks items up by SKU, so `remove` now does the same.\n\nAfter the fix, `python3 -m shop.demo` prints `1`: only the Gadget line is left. All 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`. None of the tests cover `Cart.remove`, which is how this bug got through. Want me to add one?",
